# Twisted Roots Merc — path redirects
#
# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ MOVE THIS FILE TO THE REPO ROOT.  It must live at ./_redirects (next to  │
# │ index.html), with no file extension.                                     │
# │   Cloudflare Pages: reads ./_redirects. Netlify: reads it too.           │
# │   GitHub Pages: IGNORES IT — GH Pages cannot do redirects at all.        │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Format:  <from>  <to>  <status>
# `*` is a splat and `:placeholder` captures one segment.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT DO — read this before you go looking for a bug
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. HTTP → HTTPS. Not possible here. On Cloudflare this is a ZONE setting:
#       Cloudflare dashboard → twistedrootsmerc.com → SSL/TLS → Edge
#       Certificates → "Always Use HTTPS" = ON
#    Also turn ON "Automatic HTTPS Rewrites" while you are on that screen.
#    (Optionally set HSTS there too — but read DEPLOY.md first, HSTS is very
#    hard to undo.)
#
# 2. www → apex. Not possible here either: Cloudflare Pages `_redirects`
#    matches on PATH only, not on hostname, so there is no way to say "only
#    when the host is www". Do it with a Redirect Rule in the zone —
#    exact click-path in DEPLOY.md section 3. On Netlify it IS possible, and
#    deploy/netlify.toml already contains that rule.
#
# The canonical host is the APEX: https://twistedrootsmerc.com
# That is not a preference — every <link rel="canonical"> in the nine pages
# and every <loc> in sitemap.xml already points at the apex. Choosing www
# would mean editing all of them. Don't.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Keep working files off the public web
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore should already keep these out of the repo entirely. These lines
# are the second lock: if someone force-adds the folder back, or ships from a
# machine with a stale .gitignore, the files still are not browsable.
#
# _parts/hq.html matters most — it is a copy of the private dashboard markup
# and would sit completely outside any /hq protection.

/_parts/*        /    301
/build.py        /    301
/fetch_stock.py  /    301
/TECH-PLAN.md    /    301
/QA-REPORT.md    /    301
/seo/*           /    301
/print/*         /    301
/README.md       /    301
/slots.json      /    301
/slots2.json     /    301
/slots3.json     /    301
/slots4.json     /    301


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Friendly short paths for print, signage and the phone
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Safe to hand out on a business card, a chalkboard or over the phone:
#   twistedrootsmerc.com/hours  → the Visit page
#   twistedrootsmerc.com/menu   → the Bakery + Kitchen page
# These are 302 (temporary) on purpose — they are marketing aliases, not the
# canonical address of the page, and a 302 will not be cached forever by a
# browser if you decide to repoint them.

/hours       /visit    302
/directions  /visit    302
/menu        /bakery   302
/food        /bakery   302
/order       /bakery   302
/lumber      /yard     302
/storm-ready /storm    302
/about       /roots    302
/contact     /visit    302


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOT NEEDED — and here is why, so nobody adds them back
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# /*  /404.html  404
#     Unnecessary on Cloudflare Pages: it serves /404.html automatically for
#     any unmatched path. (Also, Pages `_redirects` does not accept 404 as a
#     status code — Netlify does, Cloudflare does not.) Just create 404.html
#     at the repo root; see DEPLOY.md section 5d.
#
# /merc.html  /merc  301
#     Unnecessary AND counterproductive: Cloudflare Pages already does this
#     redirect itself, unconditionally, and you cannot turn it off. Adding
#     your own rule risks a redirect loop. See DEPLOY.md → "The one big
#     gotcha".
#
# /hq  ...  anything
#     Do NOT try to hide the dashboard with a redirect. A redirect is a
#     suggestion to a browser, not a lock. Use Cloudflare Access.
